  "id": "unconditioned-response",
  "term": "unconditioned response",
  "definition": "An unconditioned response is an innate, reflex-like reaction that is directly triggered by a relevant stimulus without prior learning. In the source example, a honeybee’s proboscis extension to sucrose is described as an unconditioned response that is naturally elicited, though its expression can still be modified by experience.",
