      "reasons": [
        "The packet only describes a specific unconditioned response in honeybees (PER/proboscis extension to sucrose) rather than establishing a general, cross-species definition of “an unconditioned response.”",
        "The definition’s claim that the response is “directly triggered … without prior learning” is not explicitly stated in the packet text; the packet instead says the response is reflexively elicited and has innately defined parameters calibrated through learning, without clearly framing “without prior learning” as a defining criterion."
